    verification writePathCensusRowsHaveARefusalBehindThemRefineGate : Test { :>> id = "0ccb10ff-1c78-4504-a536-e98123bfad44"; :>> title = "Sprint 701 refine gate (DoR)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Chartered by D0426 (unabusedHumanGatekeepersAreDissolved, human-accepted): the census that Decision reads to say which controls bind whom is only as true as its rows, and issue449 is a row that was false of the verb it named for two days (issue448 the incident). Two points: one const table with a lookup, three source-reading tests, one census test, one lookup in ledger_refused and two match arms. DoR: frontier item per keel show whats-next after sprint 700 cleared the CI red; the pair is the DoD's own (named 2026-09-10, before the registry existed); the probe is run by editing the table and the row, never the test. NOT A PROCESS CHANGE: no new refusal, gate or hook - the refusals already in code are enumerated and held; the one new ledger fact (record:tool-output-prose) is an existing refusal that gained its ledger line."; }
