    verification writePathCensusRowsHaveARefusalBehindThemRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "837b4be1-1170-439a-8abe-08b3c12ae732"; :>> title = "Sprint 701 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Two findings, both tracked. First: record:tool-output-prose was a real refusal (WriteError::InjectedToolOutput, issue255/issue256) with no ledger_refused call on its path - grep tool-output-prose .keel/metrics/hooks.jsonl -> 0 lines across both incidents, so the fire-ledger could count nothing for a control that had fired twice. The two match arms fix this instance by hand; a source-reading test cannot see a registered refusal whose path never reaches ledger_refused. issue527 tracks that residual, resolved by dcEveryRegisteredRefusalLedgersAFire: a test that drives each registered refusal through its verb against a fixture and reads its ledger line back. Second: while reading reject's channel for its rows, reject_decision_locked (write.rs) was found to call no refuse_ai_judgment where accept_decision does (write.rs:1935), reject is in neither HUMAN_ONLY_WRITE_COMMANDS nor HUMAN_AUTHORITY_COMMANDS, and confirmationAuthenticityRule reads resultJudgedByHuman(Accept) only (rules.sysml:114) - an AI actor can record a human's rejection with nothing refusing it at any layer. issue526 (High) tracks it, resolved by dcRejectIsHumanJudgedAtTheWriteAndTheRule, a CR because the rule and the command lists change. D0131 avoidable-issue scan: issue449 itself was avoidable at D0426 by asking, when a row was written, what code the row named - the registry is that question made structural; issue526 was avoidable at D0393 by holding reject to accept's write-layer checks when its synopsis claimed accept's rules - the control_structure test that would have caught it only iterates the list reject was left out of; no further item."; }
    // RAN: KEEL suite --touched . -> DETACHED; launched; exit=0; TOUCHED RECEIPT: outcome=pass passed=794 failed=0 seconds=1074 at=1789332683 launch=1789331604 (at>launch: ok)
    part writePathCensusRowsHaveARefusalBehindThemRetroGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "684a672c-f4c6-465b-8564-bcab02c3bf03"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::proposed; :>> judgedAgainst = "4b7467c"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
